Centred the login page and gave the callback and the first-login wait the same card. `@plone/components`' `Container` only takes auto margins when it is given one of its own width modifiers — `narrow`, `default`, `layout` — and the login card is sized by this add-on instead, so it had none and sat against the left edge of the window. The callback and the first-login route were worse off still: they rendered a bare `<div>` with no container at all, so their one line of status text was glued to the window border.

Both now render inside `LoginPanel`, which is what `volto-authomatic` does with its own OAuth callback: it is the login page one redirect later, so it is the same card. `LoginPanel`'s description strip became optional, since neither has anything to put in it and an empty strip is still a coloured band. @ericof
